  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Fig. 13, 'Example decision-support logic matrix from DAK for HIV'. A table with four columns: activity ID and name, decision table ID, decision table description, and reference/source. It has six rows, HIV.DT.01 to HIV.DT.06: check for serious illness; test for HIV using the testing algorithm; determine retest recommendation; PrEP eligibility check; determine PEP or PrEP regimen; and screen for TB. Each row cites the WHO consolidated guideline section it is drawn from — for example the 2019 consolidated guidelines on HIV testing services, and its figures on universal HIV testing and early infant diagnosis. Source: WHO (31).",
